{"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Hamiltonian path, or nil when there is none (or no vertex): the first one a depth-first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backtracking search finds, from each vertex in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, extending through each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"code":"outEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in order to an unvisited vertex (Mathematica "},{"code":"FindHamiltonianPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts only subtrees with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left without a usable predecessor or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"successor), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n searches."}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Tours"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"hamiltonianPath","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks4PathV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Path"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"